        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "25d36491-c94d-5b7f-9af5-0ecea2202e03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1924 Grand Prix season, Indianapolis 500, French Grand Prix, Italian Grand Prix\n- Organizations: International Sporting Commission, AIACR, Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile\n- Places: Europe, North America, Lyon, Monza\n- Topics: Grand Prix motor racing, Formula One championships\n\nFacts:\n- The 1924 Grand Prix season featured Grand Prix motor racing in Europe and North America.\n- In 1924, the International Sporting Commission of the AIACR designated the Indianapolis 500 as a Grand Épreuve.\n- In 1924, the French Grand Prix held in Lyon and the Italian Grand Prix at Monza were also Grand Épreuves.\n- The French Grand Prix, formerly called the Grand Prix de l'ACF, is held as part of the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile's annual Formula One automobile racing championships.\n- The French Grand Prix is one of the oldest motor races in the world.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "69a1a23b-b410-571e-84c4-ec3d590f34e9",
        "text": "Page: 1924 Grand Prix season. Sentence: The 1924 Grand Prix season again saw Grand Prix motor racing in Europe and North America.\nPage: 1924 Grand Prix season. Sentence: The Indianapolis 500 was again designated a Grand Épreuve by the International Sporting Commission of the AIACR, along with the French Grand Prix, held in Lyon and the Italian Grand Prix at Monza.\nPage: French Grand Prix. Sentence: The French Grand Prix (French: \"Grand Prix de France\" ), formerly known as the Grand Prix de l'ACF, is a race held as part of the Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile's annual Formula One automobile racing championships.\nPage: French Grand Prix. Sentence: It is one of the oldest motor races in the world.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
